\item  For any $\alpha,\beta \in  \mathbb{F} $ and any $ f, g \in V$, $\mathfrak{d}(\alpha · f + \beta · g) \leq \max\{\mathfrak{d}(f), \mathfrak{d}(g)\}$. Thus, the set
of functions $f \in V$ with $\mathfrak{d}(f) \leq  d$ is an $ F$-linear subspace which we denote as $\mathcal{C}(V,D)_d$.
