\begin{theorem}\label{thm:main_mat_thm}
    In the case where $\mathcal{C}_1 = \mathcal{C}_2 = \mathcal{C}(G,D)$ where $G,D$ are chosen from a function field with genus $g$ and $T$ is the matrix multiplication tensor corresponding to $(\chi,\nu, \zeta )$, we have that 
    \begin{equation*}
       \mathcal{R}(T,N) = 2 R(\chi, \nu, \zeta)-1+g.
    \end{equation*}
    In the particular case where $\chi = \nu = \zeta = m$ for some $m$ we have that 
    \begin{equation*}
       \mathcal{R}(T,N) = 2 m^{\omega }-1+g;
    \end{equation*}
    \emph{i.e.,}
    our scheme performs coded matrix multiplication up to a factor of 2 and additive term $g$ of the theoretically optimal complexity.

\end{theorem}




