We can then once again transform this formula into an equivalent MLP $f$, which is possible since, as mentioned before, any Boolean circuit can be transformed into an MLP. More generally, this construction is formalized as follows. Let $X_c$ denote the set of variables that are not mentioned in $t_n$. Then, $\phi'$ will be defined as:

\begin{equation}
\begin{aligned}
    \phi^{(i)}:=\phi[x_j\to x_j^i, \text{ for all } x_j \in X_c] \\
