\emph{Proof.} We will demonstrate how $H_{\mathcal{D}_p}(S,k)$ can be computed in polynomial time. This will be done using a dynamic programming algorithm that computes a portion of this sum, utilizing the notation of $DP$. Specifically, for all $i\in\mathbb{N}$, $\ell\in\mathbb{N}_0$ such that $1\leq i-\ell\leq i\leq n$, and for all $C\in\mathbb{Z}$, we define:

