\begin{lemma}
	\label{MSR-k-perceptron-S2Pcomplete, berman2002complexity}
	The MSR query for a $k$-ensemble of Perceptrons is \StoPComplexity-Complete.
\end{lemma}

\emph{Proof.} \textbf{Membership.}
We establish membership in para-$\Sigma^P_2$ using the direct definition of the complexity class since we can non-deterministically guess a subset $S$ and then utilize a coNP oracle to verify whether $S$ is sufficient.

\textbf{Hardness.} We will equivalently show that the \emph{MSR} query for an ensemble of $k=5$ 
Perceptrons is \StoPComplexity-Hard. First, we will present the 
\emph{Generalized Subset Sum} problem, which is known to be 
\StoPCompleteComplexity-complete~\cite{schaefer2002completeness}.

