This provides direct proof that computing the Shapley value under a uniform distribution (and consequently for the fully factorized distribution) is as difficult as the model counting problem. It remains to be shown that the model counting problem for an ensemble of $k$-decision trees is \#W[1]-Complete, when parameterized by $k$. Since we have already established that the \emph{CC} query for a $k$-ensemble of decision trees is \#W[1]-Complete, we can demonstrate an FPT many-one reduction from the model counting problem to the computation of the \emph{CC} query.


