The completion count seeks the number of assignments where the complement of $S$ (which, in this case, includes all possible assignments) results in a classification of $1$. Thus, if $f(\x) = 1$, we have $\#f = \#CC(f, \x, S)$, and if $f(\x) = 0$, we have $\#f = 2^n - \#CC(f, \x, S)$, concluding the reduction.

